  "title": "Week 43: Riigikogu",
  "date": "2024-10-25T21:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "Week 43: Riigikogu\n\nThis week is the mid-term. That means I have a week off. But a lot things happened this week.\n\n\n\nI went to the Estonian Parliament to do a visit. It is a 246 year building. But inside of it is neoclassical decoration. there are 101 seats, elected every 4 years. During the visit, someone asked me, how many seats in the Chinese parliament. I think it is a simple question. But I don't know. So I checked only. The nearest institution that is similar to the parliament is the standing committee of China's Central congress. It has 175 seats with 5 years term.\n\n\n\nLinus kicked a lot Russian accounts out of the Linux community. A big shock in open source community. Many people believe it will ruin the open source community. But I think it still need time to see the result.\n\nI touched pixel watch for the first time. I really like the design. But I worry the pebble shell can not last long.\n\nMac mini is like twice price here than PinDuoDuo. I know I will have 2 years' warranty. But it is a lot of money. Apple is going to announce new Mac mini. I hope it is not what I want. So I can hang out more not to decide to find a job.\n\nExtraordinary\n\nI finished the second season of Extraordinary. Expecting the third season.\n\nBolt scooter\n\nMy first try on bolt scooter. Super scared of the speed.",
